dotnet aspnet-codegenerator controller Identity -dc ApplicationDbContext -u ApplicationDbContext.Users -m /Views/Identity/Account/Index.cshtml -v /Views/Identity/Account/Login.cshtml -o Controllers/Account
```

 5. Run the application and navigate to the login page. You can now use the built-in Identity framework to handle user authentication and authorization.

Note: Using the built-in Identity framework is the recommended approach for password protecting an ASP.NET Core website, as it provides a secure and flexible way to manage user accounts and roles. Using `.htaccess` or `web.config` files for password protection is not recommended, as they are not designed for use with ASP.NET Core applications and may not work as expected.
